{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788193072,"nonce":"UXYrEmlP8uYYjKDcurOuIpnAIjk=","title":"combat-report: read the battle log by field, never by the game's sentence builder","message":"Evan asked for proof that something USEFUL could be concluded from RimWorld's\ncombat logs before anything was filed. It can. Filed on that basis.\n\nWHAT IS DERIVABLE (confirmed by an investigation that built them from source)\n\n- **Who shot whom, with what.** Attacker, target, weapon and body part are all\n  recorded per entry.\n- **What killed a specific pawn** — a reconstructable chain of events for one\n  casualty, not an anecdote.\n- A defensible per-participant scoreboard.\n\nThose came out of reading the `BattleLogEntry_*` fields directly. They did NOT\ncome from the game's own prose, which matters — see below.\n\n**THE OBVIOUS SHORTCUT IS A TRAP. Do not use it.**\n`RimWorld/ITab_Pawn_Log_Utility.cs` `GenerateLogLinesFor` is poisoned twice:\n\n1. It returns `tmpLogLines`, a `private static List` it `Clear()`s on entry — so\n   calling it wipes the open Log tab's cache out from under the UI. Same\n   static-aliasing class as `ListerThings.ThingsMatchingFilter`.\n2. It calls `Battle.GetName()` per battle header, which **consumes RNG and\n   writes a scribed field**. That method has exactly ONE call site in the entire\n   game — a mouse click — which is the only reason Ludeon gets away with it.\n\n`LogEntry.ToGameStringFromPOV` is safer (its RNG guard is real) but still not a\nfoundation: it reaches `PawnsFinder.…FreeColonistsAndPrisoners`, which `Clear()`s\nand refills a static list — the exact Class E hazard that produced AutoRimmer's\nlive \"Collection was modified\" bug in 2.1 — plus a nested grammar resolve, an\nunbounded `ColoredText.cache`, and `GenLabel.labelDictionary` writes. If prose\nis ever wanted for ONE entry it is the right way to get it, cached and refreshed\nonly when the change-detector moves. It is not the base layer.\n\nAlso confirmed: `PlayLogEntry_Interaction` and friends each add a REDUNDANT,\nunguarded `Rand.PushState`/`PopState` with **no try/finally**, so a throw inside\nleaks a frame and leaves the stream seeded until `Root.Update` repairs it. The\n`BattleLogEntry_*` classes do not do this. Another reason the social log is the\nwrong thing to build on.\n\nFREE CHANGE DETECTION, and it fits the idiom already in the codebase.\n`RimWorld/ITab_Pawn_Log.cs` `FillTab` regenerates only when\n`Pawn_RecordsTracker.LastBattleTick` or `PlayLog.LastTick` moves — two pure int\nreads, no allocation. That gives `combat-report` a \"nothing has happened since\nyou last asked\" fast path matching `digest`/`journal`'s `since` shape.\n\nMinor, load-bearing details: only TWO `LogEntryDef`s exist game-wide\n(`MeleeAttack`, `SandInEyes`) and `LogEntry.def` is null on most entries — do\nnot key anything on it. Any reflection cache must key on the CONCRETE type:\n`PlayLogEntry_InteractionSinglePawn` does NOT inherit from\n`PlayLogEntry_Interaction`, it re-declares its own fields.\n\nINFORMATION-LEAK POLICY still applies. PawnSafe's rule (do not confirm the\nexistence of pawns the player cannot see) governs what a report may say about\nenemies. Fog-filter participants; the log knowing something is not permission to\nreport it.\n\nWHY IT IS FILED NOW RATHER THAN WHEN NEEDED: the research is done and would go\nstale. The consumer is **4.2** (the play loop) — \"we just took casualties, what\nnow\" is the decision this feeds. Nothing today acts on it, so this is not urgent\nand should not jump the queue.\n\nAcceptance\n- A `combat-report` verb built on field reads via a `BattleSafe`-style\n  reflection layer, with `GenerateLogLinesFor` and `ToGameStringFromPOV` named\n  in its forbidden list and WHY.\n- Answers, for the last engagement: participants, a per-pawn scoreboard, and a\n  casualty chain naming attacker and weapon.\n- Enemy participants fog-filtered per PawnSafe.\n- The `LastBattleTick` fast path demonstrated: two calls with no fight between\n  them, the second returning \"unchanged\" without walking entries.\n- Zero red errors, and a save-file diff showing the read wrote nothing.","files":null}]}